    bottomLine:
      "The best all-around treadmill for home use if you want iFit-powered training and don't mind the subscription.",
    description:
      "The Commercial 1750 earns the top spot in this guide for a simple reason: nothing else here matches its combination of power, incline range, and interactive training on paper. The <strong>3.75 CHP motor</strong> is a strong continuous rating for a home machine, with headroom for sustained incline intervals at running pace. The <strong>-3% to 15% incline/decline range</strong> is the widest in this roundup and genuinely changes how a treadmill workout feels, letting you simulate downhill running instead of just flat sprints. The 14-inch rotating touchscreen pivots for off-treadmill floor workouts, and iFit's trainer-led runs through locations such as Iceland and the Rockies are designed to make sessions less tedious than staring at a blank wall. The FlexSelect cushioning system lets you toggle between a softer, joint-friendly setting and a firmer, more responsive one, which is useful if you move between walking days and tempo runs. The catch is cost: between the machine itself, typically <strong>$1,999 to $2,499</strong>, and the iFit subscription needed to unlock adaptive coaching and scenery, this is a real investment. It's also a large, heavy machine that two people should handle when folding or moving. For serious home exercisers who want a gym-quality experience at home, though, it's the clear pick.",
  },
  {
    id: "sole-f80",
    name: "Sole F80",
    editorialScore: 4.7,
    category: "Heavy-Duty Home Treadmill",
    badge: "Best Build Quality",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Sole+F80+Treadmill&tag=sktiger-20",
    pros: [
      "Oversized 22 x 60 inch deck fits taller runners comfortably",
      "375 lb weight capacity, among the highest in this class",
      "Cushioned deck noticeably reduces joint impact on longer runs",
      "Reputation for commercial-grade durability in a home-sized unit",
      "No subscription required to access core training features",
    ],
    cons: [
