    bottomLine:
      "The smartest balance of premium features and price for most buyers shopping in the mid-to-premium range.",
    description:
      "The 7.8 AT sits right in the sweet spot between budget machines and true premium models, and it earns our pick as the best value in the premium tier. The <strong>10-inch HD touchscreen</strong> supports Bluetooth pairing with training apps for streamed workout content. Horizon's frame construction is the main selling point: it is built for HIIT-style sessions that alternate walking recovery with sprint intervals, where lighter budget frames are more prone to side-to-side wobble. The <strong>0-15% incline range</strong> matches machines costing hundreds more, which suits trainer-guided hill workouts. At <strong>3.5 CHP</strong>, the motor is rated for sustained running, and Horizon's variable-response cushioning system, which is firmer under the heel and softer at midfoot, is designed as a middle ground rather than the plush give of the Sole F80. Assembly is the one place this machine asks more of you; as a larger, feature-rich frame, budget for the upper end of typical assembly times with two people. Priced between <strong>$1,599 and $1,899</strong>, the 7.8 AT offers most of what you'd want from a premium treadmill without the premium-tier price tag, which is exactly why it lands so high on our list.",
  },
  {
    id: "bowflex-treadmill-22",
    name: "Bowflex Treadmill 22",
    editorialScore: 4.4,
    category: "Interactive Home Cardio",
    badge: "Best Large Touchscreen",
    amazonUrl:
