        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">4. How to Choose the Right Treadmill for YOUR Home</h2>
        <p>
          The "best" treadmill depends entirely on who's using it and how. Here's how we'd narrow the field based on your specific situation.
        </p>

        <h3>By Body Type and Height</h3>
        <p>
          If you're under 5'8", most decks in this guide, including the Schwinn 810's smaller 20 x 55 inch surface, will feel comfortable. Taller users, especially anyone over 6 feet, should prioritize a <strong>60-inch or longer deck</strong>, which rules out the Schwinn and points toward the Sole F80, Bowflex Treadmill 22, or NordicTrack Commercial 1750, all of which offer more room for a full stride at running speeds. Foot width and stride pattern matter too; wider, more aggressive strides benefit disproportionately from the extra deck length, even for users of average height.
        </p>

        <h3>By Primary Use: Walking vs. Running vs. HIIT</h3>
        <p>
          Walkers and light joggers can get excellent value from lower-horsepower machines like the <strong>Schwinn 810</strong> or <strong>Horizon 7.0 AT</strong>, both of which handle everyday walking workouts without issue and cost considerably less than running-focused machines. Regular runners should look toward <strong>3.5 CHP or higher</strong> motors, favoring the Sole F80, Horizon 7.8 AT, or NordicTrack Commercial 1750. If your workouts lean toward HIIT with frequent, sharp speed and incline changes, prioritize a treadmill with fast-responding incline motors and a stable frame, where the Horizon 7.8 AT and NordicTrack Commercial 1750 stand out on paper. Anyone training for a specific race or event should also weigh top speed; most home treadmills cap out between 10 and 12 mph, which is plenty for the vast majority of runners but worth checking if you're training for competitive paces.
        </p>

        <h3>By Space Constraints</h3>
        <p>
          Apartment dwellers and anyone working with a small room should look for machines with a <strong>folding deck and a compact footprint</strong>. The ProForm Pro 2000 and Horizon 7.0 AT both fold down efficiently and take up less floor space than the Bowflex Treadmill 22, which has the largest overall footprint in this guide and needs a genuinely dedicated area. Don't forget to account for the space needed to safely step off the machine and walk around it during setup or cleaning, not just the treadmill's own footprint when folded flat against a wall.
        </p>

        <h3>By Household: Multiple Users</h3>
        <p>
          If more than one person, especially people of different heights and weights, will regularly use the machine, prioritize a <strong>higher weight capacity</strong> and a more adjustable incline/cushioning system so each user can tailor the experience. The Sole F80's 375 lb capacity and adjustable cushioning make it a strong pick for multi-user households, as does the NordicTrack Commercial 1750's FlexSelect system. Multi-user households should also weigh how easily each person can save and switch between individual profiles, since re-entering age, weight, and goal data every session gets old fast.
        </p>

        <h3>By Budget Tier</h3>
        <p>
          Under $1,000, the <strong>Schwinn 810</strong> and <strong>Horizon 7.0 AT</strong> deliver the most reliable full-size experience. Between $1,000 and $1,500, the <strong>ProForm Pro 2000</strong> is our top pick for interactive training value. From $1,500 to $2,000, the <strong>Sole F80</strong> and <strong>Horizon 7.8 AT</strong> both deliver premium-feeling builds. Above $2,000, the <strong>NordicTrack Commercial 1750</strong> and <strong>Bowflex Treadmill 22</strong> represent the top of the home-use market covered in this guide. Wherever you land, remember that sale pricing is common in this category, especially around major shopping holidays, so it's worth checking current pricing before assuming a machine is out of your range.
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-8">
