        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buyers Make</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The same four buying errors come up again and again, and none of them are about the machines themselves.</p>
        <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Choosing on spec sheet alone</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Deck feel, console responsiveness, and noise are the things owners actually notice daily, and none appear in a specification table. Where you can, stand on the machine before buying.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating peak horsepower as the motor rating</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Continuous-duty horsepower is the number that describes sustained work. Peak figures make weaker motors look competitive with stronger ones.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Forgetting the subscription renews</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Machines that bundle a first year of iFit or JRNY bill annually after. Budget for year two before comparing them against subscription-free rivals.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Skipping the break-in and maintenance routine</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The first 20 miles seat the belt, and periodic lubrication keeps it from dragging. Owners who skip both report problems years earlier than those who do not.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
